# Caddy in front of UwUMail Server, to go with compose.proxy.yaml in this folder.
#
# The upstream is UwUMail's proxy listener on port 8080. Never point a reverse proxy at UwUMail's
# port 80: that one only redirects to https://<host name>/, which behind a proxy goes round in
# circles.
#
# Nothing else to set: reverse_proxy passes the Host header on unchanged and sets X-Forwarded-For
# and X-Forwarded-Proto by itself. That is exactly what UwUMail reads, once Caddy's address is in
# http.trusted_proxies.

mail.example.com {
	reverse_proxy uwumail:8080
}

# Other names that have to reach UwUMail too, as soon as their DNS records point here:
# mta-sts.<domain> of every domain with MTA-STS on (UwUMail picks the domain from the host name),
# and autoconfig.<domain> and autodiscover.<domain>, where Thunderbird and Outlook look up the
# settings. Caddy gets their certificates.
#
# UwUMail's own Let's Encrypt certificate for the mail ports (tls.mode = "acme") is checked
# through Caddy as well, name by name. Names that mail apps connect to, like imap.<domain> or
# smtp.<domain>, only join it when they are listed here too.
#
# mta-sts.example.com, autoconfig.example.com, autodiscover.example.com {
# 	reverse_proxy uwumail:8080
# }

# A server at home behind a UwUMail Gateway (setup B): Caddy is not in the public path. The name
# points to the gateway, whose ports 80 and 443 end in UwUMail through the tunnel, so UwUMail
# needs no entry here, and Caddy could not get a public certificate for the name anyway. The
# simplest is no local DNS entry for the name: use the gateway from home too.
#
# Only with a local DNS entry that points the name at this machine inside your own network: Caddy
# can serve it with a certificate from its own CA. Every device then has to trust Caddy's root
# certificate. Through the gateway UwUMail sends HSTS, and a browser that has seen it does not let
# you click through a certificate warning for the name. The other way is a Caddy build with a DNS
# plugin and the DNS challenge instead of "tls internal".
#
# mail.example.com {
# 	tls internal
# 	reverse_proxy uwumail:8080
# }
